Z||000000||Ferrari355||04-30-2000||10:39 PM||||hey evetybody, my dad let me get on to ask you guys a ? Ok a long time ago i told you guys about buying an 86 Fiero GT from a JUNKYARD. Well they are auctioning off everything this saturday and me and my dad are planning on going out there to look at the fiero. Ok, I was wondering if an automatic Tranny from an 84 fiero SE with bolt up to an 86 Fiero gt V6 which is a manual if we sqitch consoles and stuff. If it doesn't could you tell me what we'll have to do. Cause we were thinking instead of taking most body panels off of the SE we could just maybe switch tranny's. Let me know, I'll check back tomorrow, storms are heading our way and it's lightening. TTYL, Bye... you can e-mail me dad at  <A HREF="mailto:BKS854@aol.com">BKS854@aol.com</A>  Great talking to you all again. BYe....||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||04-30-2000||10:47 PM||||The fiero trannies all mix and match. Not rocket science but not fun either. The years involved make a bit more of a pain.<P>You need the right flywheel/flexplate for the motor. (Make sure you remove the pilot bushing from the motor when changing to automatic. Sometimes its there even tho it ain't used.)<P>You also need the right PROM for the ECM. and a few wiring changes so the Torque converter clutch can lock. These are all parts that will need to be for the right motor and year. (You can't put a PROM from a 86 or 87 4 cyl in an 84. all 3 ECM are diferant.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-30-2000||10:48 PM||||No can do! You'll need a different fly wheel/flex plate for the automatic.  I've heard of going from automatic to manual, not the other way around.  Dig deep for the $$$.||||reg||3
Z||000003||lowCG||04-30-2000||10:58 PM||||No problem,a little work,but maybe someone who's actually done this on a Fiero will anty up some info on exactly what you need besides the flexplate,cables,etc.<BR>Have done this on other GM cars with no problems at all.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||04-30-2000||11:46 PM||||Wouldn't you need to exchange radiator, run coolant lines for the AT, and swap computers? If so, that just seems like a God-awful amount of work for a slush-box.<BR>Maybe i'm missing something. What is wrong w/ the 86 gt? You want to put the AT in the 86, right? What is the thing about taking the body panels off of the 84? I;m soo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> confused Alex!<BR>P.S., Y'all coming down to Norman on May 20 for the Fiero show? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||05-01-2000||09:56 AM||||Id be willing to bet that the main cooling lines are already in place, as It would be harder to build some cars with them and some with out on an assembly line.<P>It is kind of a confusing question tho..It sounds like the 86GT may have a good motor/tranny but the body is screwed and the 84 is in good shape other than engine/tranny.  <P>You could drop the entire engine/tranny and swap all of the cars wiring from the front bulkhead to the interface to the engine harness and voila.  Its a tedious job, but if you take your time and remove center console plus all dashboard components, it can be done.<P>Or you could just swap the body panels from the 84 to the 86, but if the 86 was in a junkyard, you could end up doing alot of legwork trying to get a title for it...||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroshop||05-01-2000||10:21 AM||||Requirements for the switch from manual to auto requires a lot of work. !. replace the flywheel with a flex plate. <BR>2. you need the wiring harness replaced, not only do you need to replace the engine wiring harness but also the main wiring harness in the car.<BR>3. you must replace the radiator and install cooling lines to the rear of the car for the transmission to cool. <BR>4. replace the ecm chip and depending on the year of the car the ecm itself.<BR>5 Go buyu an aoutamatc car and not have to do all the work.||||reg||1
