Z||000008||Dan86gt3.8||05-02-2000||04:49 AM||||alex,<BR>when i converted over to the 3.8 I went from a manual to the auto that comes with the 3.8.  What we had to do was pull the brake/clutch pedal assembly (all one piece and put in an automatic brake pedal.  My dad allso pulled some coolant lines from a junkyard, and the car originally started out life as an auto so the radiator had the trany cooler in it.  of course you will need an auto shifter and the correct cables.  You will also need a little gismo that goes on the steering wheel column( have nop clue what its called but can describe it to a t and know how to take it out/ put it on) that locks the shifter when its in park.  But when i did it it was entirely different situation.  I have no clue what you need to do with the wiring or the ecm.  But as far as the mechanics go you need thoose things and go ahead and make it easy on yourself and take out the whole console area, drivers side dash, steering column, etc, etc.  Alll this crap was out when I did it and made thins very simple!||||reg||1
